{"changes":["cmd/schema.go (new): schemaReport/schemaCommand/schemaFlag types and buildSchemaReport, which walks the command tree and describes every non-hidden command: path, intent group, mutation risk, usage, flags (name, shorthand, type, default, repeatable, required, description), and subcommands. Help and completion are excluded: they are cobra's, not this project's contract.","cmd/schema.go: readOnlyCommands is an explicit allow-list for mutation risk rather than a derivation from the presentation group. Deriving it from the group was wrong: `feedback` sits in Utility beside `version` yet writes drafts and opens GitHub issues, and the plugin lifecycle commands (configure, install) carry no risk metadata at all. Under-reporting a mutation is the dangerous direction, so an unlisted command reports as mutating.","cmd/schema.go: subcommands inherit their root ancestor's group and risk, so `draft validate` is classified rather than appearing unclassified.","cmd/root.go: registered the command. cmd/help_groups.go: added `schema` to the Utility group so the help grouping and the schema report agree; cmd/help_groups_test.go membership list updated to match."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Added `eka schema [--json]`, generating a machine-readable description of the whole command surface from the live cobra tree.","tests":["cmd/schema_test.go (new), five tests: every registered command appears in the report; mutation risk is correct for the commands that write and the ones that only read (including feedback new/publish and every plugin-provided command); a known flag is described with its type; the reported flag set matches each command's actual definitions in both directions; two runs produce byte-identical JSON so a caching agent sees no churn.","go test ./cmd/ -run TestSchemaReport -\u003e all five PASS. go test ./cmd/ -run 'TestCommandGroup|TestGroups|TestSchema|TestLanding|TestRootHelp' -\u003e ok.","go build ./... , go vet ./cmd/ , gofmt -l . -\u003e clean.